# Machine-local paths — never commit
.jenga_paths

# Project-scoped scratch dir used by ad-hoc helpers (legacy: distribute-changes.sh)
.jenga_tmp/

# Ad-hoc smoke-test scratch space (e.g. fake consumer installs)
.tmp/

# Python temp files
**/__pycache__

# fine tuning jobs
jobs/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
*.local
*.pid
node_modules/

# npm pack artifacts (e.g. from manual verification runs like E26_S09_T03)
*.tgz

# Jenga runtime files (machine-local, auto-generated)
mcp/router/.pid
mcp/router/.session.json

# Worktrees
**/worktrees/

# Public mirror scratch worktree (used by /mirror-public)
.mirror-worktrees/

# Claude/Copilot session artefacts
agents/.agents/

# Running dashboard's recorded port (project/queue/dashboard-port.json, E47_S08_T03): machine-local, written
# when the dashboard starts and removed when it stops.
project/queue/dashboard-port.json
project/queue/dashboard-port.json.*.tmp

# Per-session handoff files (project/queue/handoffs/) are transient,
# single-use signals consumed and deleted by hooks/on_session_end.sh
# immediately after routing (see templates/SCRUM_BOARD_SCHEMA.md's
# handoffs/ section: "A file must not persist once it has been
# consumed."). They must never be durable git artifacts — E37_S01_T02
# found ~25 of them had been committed anyway (swept up by unrelated
# `git add -A` commits before the hook ever consumed this directory) and
# accumulated into a resurrection hazard: a later, correct consumer would
# treat them as live signals for work already fully shipped. This rule
# structurally prevents recurrence rather than relying on every agent to
# remember not to `git add` this directory.
project/queue/handoffs/*.json
!project/queue/handoffs/.gitkeep

# Conversational elicitation state (project/queue/elicitation-state/,
# skills/uncharted/scripts/elicitation-state.sh — E20_S08_T03) is
# session-scratch resumability data for /uncharted's convergence loop, not a
# durable artifact — the durable output of a converged elicitation is the
# graph write (project/knowledge-graph/graph.json) and the [ARCH]-tagged
# board item, both written separately. Mirrors the handoffs/ rule above for
# the same reason: it must never become a durable git artifact that a later
# session could mistake for a live in-progress signal.
project/queue/elicitation-state/*.json
!project/queue/elicitation-state/.gitkeep

# resolved_context digest files (project/queue/context/ — E49_S01_T02) are
# transient, single-use handoff payloads written by scripts/write-context-digest.sh
# and consumed (read + deleted) by scripts/consume-context-digest.sh, with
# scripts/sweep-stale-context-digests.sh as an age-based backstop for a digest
# whose intended receiver never consumes it. Mirrors the handoffs/ rule above
# for the same reason: a digest is a per-session scratch payload referenced by
# a handoff's resolved_context field, not a durable record — the durable
# record is the handoff/board state that referenced it. See
# templates/SCRUM_BOARD_SCHEMA.md's resolved_context subsection.
project/queue/context/*.json
!project/queue/context/.gitkeep

# Pre-flight checklist tick state (project/queue/checklist-ticks/,
# scripts/checklist.sh tick — E67_S02_T03) is private operational state: the
# shared persistent.json, one run-<digest>.json per run id, and the transient
# *.lock.d / .tmp-* entries the lock and the write-then-rename leave beside
# them. A persistent tick is meant to outlive a session, which is exactly why
# it must never become a durable git artifact (a committed tick would satisfy
# a checklist item on every clone). Mirrors the handoffs/ rule above; the
# directory is also blocklisted for the public mirror via project/queue/.
project/queue/checklist-ticks/*
!project/queue/checklist-ticks/.gitkeep

# Situation marker (project/queue/checklist-markers/,
# scripts/checklist-marker.sh — E67_S04_T01) is the transient "which
# lifecycle phase is this session in" value the enforcing hook reads: one
# marker-<digest>.json per session key, plus the *.lock.d / .tmp-* entries the
# lock and the write-then-rename leave beside them. It is meaningful only for
# the session that wrote it and only until its TTL expires, so committing one
# would gate every clone on a phase that is not running. Sibling of the
# checklist-ticks/ rule above; also blocklisted for the public mirror via
# project/queue/.
project/queue/checklist-markers/*
!project/queue/checklist-markers/.gitkeep

# Workflow run state (project/data/workflow-runs/, E80_S02) is private
# operational state: one workflow run per state file, plus the transient
# *.lock.d / .tmp-* entries the lock and the write-then-rename leave beside
# them. A run is meant to span sessions, which is exactly why it
# must never become a durable git artifact: a committed run would be
# resumed on every clone. Mirrors the checklist-ticks/ rule above. Ignore the
# subdirectory only, never project/data/ itself, which is partly tracked
# (baselines.json). Also blocklisted for the public mirror in .publicignore,
# because project/data/ is not covered by the project/queue/ entry there.
project/data/workflow-runs/*
!project/data/workflow-runs/.gitkeep

# One-time dependency-audit opt-in notice marker (scripts/audit-notice.sh, E85_S04_T02):
# records that this clone's user has already seen the notice, so it is per-user
# state and must never be committed. File only (and its transient .tmp/.lock.d
# siblings); project/data/ itself stays partly tracked.
project/data/audit-notice-shown
project/data/audit-notice-shown.*

# Workflow artifacts (project/data/workflow-artifacts/, E80_S04) are deliberately
# NOT ignored: a sprint or roadmap artifact is a deliverable that collaborators
# and the dashboard timeline read, and an ignored location would make `latest`
# return nothing on a fresh clone. The directory is tracked via its .gitkeep, so
# do not widen any project/data/ rule to cover it. The cost is that every run is
# retained; pruning is a future concern. It is blocklisted for the public mirror
# in .publicignore, because project-specific plans must not leak downstream.

# Per-session execution ledger (project/queue/execution-ledger.jsonl,
# skills/j-break/scripts/record-execution.sh — E44_S09) is append-only,
# queue-like transient state: one line per terminal task status a /do, /dooo
# or /jenga session wrote, keyed by session key, read by `/break status` to
# tell "ran this session" from "done earlier". It is meaningful only to the
# machine and sessions that wrote it, so it must never become a durable git
# artifact. Already blocklisted for the public mirror via project/queue/
# (.publicignore). Rotation is a deferred follow-up.
project/queue/execution-ledger.jsonl

# Transient per-session queue files (project/queue/) — concurrency slot
# holders, conflict notes, bundle and epic-lock state, and the session handoff
# scratch file. Each is written for one live session or dispatch and removed
# or superseded when it ends; none is a durable record, so none may be
# committed. The durable trigger logs (scrum_triggers.jsonl,
# tester_triggers.jsonl, project_summary_updates.jsonl) and the .gitkeep
# placeholders are deliberately NOT listed here.
project/queue/.session_handoff.json
project/queue/bundle-*.json
project/queue/concurrency-slots-*.json
project/queue/conflict-*.md
project/queue/epic-lock-*.json

# Per-session perceived-branch state (project/queue/perceived-branch/, E78_S01):
# one file per live session, removed at SessionEnd; never a durable record.
project/queue/perceived-branch/

# Per-task commit ref store (project/queue/commit-refs/, scripts/task-commit-ref.sh): one JSON file per task holding
# the ref captured from the user's branch and the frozen ref. Per-machine working state like handoffs/ above, never
# history. The whole directory is listed, not *.json, so the script's temp files and its .lock.d lock directories cannot
# be committed by accident. Already blocklisted for the public mirror via project/queue/ (.publicignore).
project/queue/commit-refs/

# E73_S01 spike: raw hook-payload logs (project/logs/spike-hook-payloads/) can contain prompt text.
# They are research artefacts only and must never be committed; only redacted summaries in the
# report leave this directory. Also blocklisted for the public mirror in .publicignore.
project/logs/spike-hook-payloads/
